  "markdown": {
    "instructions": [
      "The PyPI package is graphifyy, with two y's. The command is graphify.",
      "/graphify . is typed in an assistant chat, not in a shell.",
      "Use only commands, flags, and endpoints shown on these pages. Do not invent one.",
      "Choose the surface before you open a page. Local is the graphifyy package on the machine: the skill, the CLI, and the ten-tool MCP. Its pages are the Guides and Reference tabs, /mcp/ (except /mcp/docs-search, which is for both), and the Local skill group in Integrations. Cloud (Graphify Cloud) is the hosted workspace and https://api.graphify.com/mcp (Streamable HTTP, OAuth, no API key). Its pages are the Graphify Cloud tab (/platform/) and the Cloud MCP group in Integrations. Concepts, troubleshooting, pricing, and /platform/local-to-cloud apply to both. Each page's source frontmatter records this as surface: local, cloud, or both. Buildkite is the CI integration.",
      "In llms.txt, tell the surface from the page path. Cloud: /platform/ and /integrations/ cloud, vscode, jetbrains, chatgpt, openclaw, vercel, other-agents, buildkite. Local: /guides/, /reference/, /mcp/overview, /mcp/shared-http, /installation, /quickstart, and /integrations/ claude-code, cursor, codex, gemini-cli, copilot, other-assistants. Everything else applies to both.",
      "The docs changelog summarizes selected graphifyy releases. The current package version is on PyPI (https://pypi.org/project/graphifyy/). The full history is https://graphify.com/changelog.",
      "The official site is https://graphify.com. These docs are https://docs.graphify.com.",
      "The local MCP server is the ten tools in the MCP tool reference and reads a graph on the machine. The hosted server is https://api.graphify.com/mcp (Streamable HTTP, OAuth, no API key). The VS Code, JetBrains, OpenClaw, Vercel, and Other Cloud agents pages, and the page ChatGPT, Codex, and Dots, use the hosted server, not the ten-tool list. Other local assistants is the local skill for clients without their own page. The page titled Graphify with Codex is the local skill.",
      "Read https://docs.graphify.com/llms.txt, then open one page's .md link. Use https://docs.graphify.com/llms-full.txt only when one page is not enough."
    ]
  },
  "styling": {
    "eyebrows": "breadcrumbs"
  },
  "redirects": [
    {
      "source": "/changelog",
      "destination": "/changelog/highlights"
    }
  ]
